# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# NOT-4 and NOT-9: the empty log takes the whole screen, and gives every
# pixel of it back.
# A single leg, and it has to be one. The key that opens the log reaches
# the program in a seam-off run, where the adventuring bar answers an
# unknown letter by stepping its own highlight, so from that moment the
# two runs differ on the bar row whatever the give-back does, and what a
# pair would measure is the highlight (#234).
# So the give-back is stated directly and more strongly: the frame after
# the log closes is the same screen as the frame before it opened.

about the log takes the whole screen and gives every pixel of it back
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel

# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), pinned by
# digest because a document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam journal
until 260000000
every 25

key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201
key N@10600
key Escape@11400

rect bar 0,190,319,199

# The log up, holding still, with nothing pressed.
same 10800-11375

# The screen before the log, back again after it: every pixel except the
# bar row. That exception was a finding - 951 pixels differed, all on that
# row, because the give-back left the highlight on the `Notes` group (#234)
# - and #330 fixed it at the splice. It stays until this leg is re-driven
# on the shorter boot (#293); rdr-bar.leg asserts the give-back whole.
equal 10600 11800 bar
